Jorgen Grahn wrote:
>
>>>> My only sacrifice gift so far has been that Magicbane (and Trollsbane,
>>>> which I don't use).  The problem now is: do I need to get crowned to
>>>> get any skill at all with Stormbringer?  And what about Werebane?

If you count the skill slots for wizard you'll see you can advance all
spell schools to max, plus dagger to expert and still have a couple of
slots left over for style points.  I very much like to get Stormbringer
and advance it to basic.

>> http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Crowning (which I should have checked
>> first -- sorry!) disagrees:
>>
>>       You will still unlock the weapon skill for the weapon you would
>>       have been given, even if you are a Wizard and receive the
>>       spellbook instead of the weapon.

*Plus* the weapon you are currently wielding!  As a wizard you can do
the sac/pray cycle with tuned luck to collect spellbooks and other
goodies.  Read each book as you get them.  Once you get + Finger of
Death carry it so you get Strombringer as the crowning gift.  In this
case carry Stormy and you'll get a rustproof +1 non-artifact runesword
instead.  But here's yet another detail not often used - Wield Werebane
whenever you pray with a chance of getting crowned.  When you get
crowned you get unrestricted in the class of your artifact gift (even if
you don't get it because it already exists) so that opens up Stormy,
plus you get unrestricted in the weapon you are currently wielding.

>>> OTOH, you may continue to sacrifice in the hope to get either Orcrist
>>> or Dragonbane, which would both make the broadsword class unrestricted.
>>
>> Oh, didn't realize those used the same skill class. In that case I'll
>> go on sacrificing for a while.  (Receiving Orcrist and being pleased
>> by it would be a new experience.)  If Arioch still doesn't want to
>> give me anything, I'll go for crowning.
>
> Anhur, I mean. And just now he gave me (after a ridiculous amount of
> sacrifices) not Orcrist, but Dragonbane.  So now I'm off to practice
> with my blessed rustproof +5 Stormbringer ...

Weapons in the same skills class with Stormy -

Broad sword - Stormbringer and Orcrist chaotic, Dragonbane unaligned.

Weapons in the same skills class with Werebane -

Sabre - Greyswandir lawfull, Werebane unaligned.

Since you are chaotic and you already have Werebane the only way to get
unrestricted for Werebane in your current game is to wield it at the
time you pray and get crowned.  It is arguably not worth the effort at
this point except for the fun of seeing it in the list.

For non-artifact weapons, runesword, silver saber, elven broadsword and
regular broadsword don't suck as melee' weapons except in comparison to
non-melee' combat and to good artifact weapons.  Having both Stormy and
Magicbane you now have little use for Werebane - It's a regular silver
saber for most purposes.

I like to run wizards with a good stack of highly enchanted elven
daggers, Magicbane wielded most of the time, Stormbringer or other heavy
melee' weapon as an alternate wield when I get myself in trouble.  My
sign of playing well is I've done several levels without switching to
Stormbringer since I finished exercising it to basic.

For a wizard I like to start my games rushing towards expert in dagger
so I can multi-fire from a stack.  Then start enhancing as many spell
schools as are available plus one slot for my heavy backup wielded
melee' weapon.


